ADR-0024 records the decision the phase actually forced: the submission's
lifecycle is written by RPC and nothing else. It also extends the ADR-0011
criterion, which until now was purely about atomicity — when a multi-row
operation becomes a boundary, the SIBLING operations of the same lifecycle go
with it, even the single-row ones, because two doors to the same state is how
one of them ends up missing a check.

Five decisions registered in spec-review: the deferred email (D-20), the
conditional stage advance and why forcing `immersion` would invent a fact
(D-21), reopening and the dead end its absence created (D-22), the catalog
migration (D-23), and the explicit start (D-24).

The permissions matrix grows a row — `onboarding.reopen`, admin only — and the
authorization matrix records `onboarding_submissions` dropping from `SIU` to
`S`.

